From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: St0neWan9 <pawamaba@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:46:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: chrome: let an embedder list its windows and open
 action popups

Plans B125 and B126. In an app that embeds Chrome's browser process and
shows its tabs itself (chrome::EmbedderOwnsUI()), there are no Browser
windows, so chrome.windows.getCurrent and getLastFocused failed ("No
current window", "No last-focused window"), chrome.windows.getAll
returned [], and chrome.action.openPopup() failed with "Could not find an
active browser window."

Adds two embedder hooks to ExtensionTabUtil:

- SetEmbedderWindowList(): the embedder's windows, most recently focused
  first, each with a window id (a SessionID value the embedder also sets
  as its tabs' window id), its profile (an incognito window: the
  off-the-record profile), focus, popup or normal type, screen bounds and
  tabs (with the active ones). GetEmbedderWindows() keeps those an
  extension may see, with the rule of windows_util::CanOperateOnWindow().
  windows.get, getCurrent (the caller's window, else the most recently
  focused one), getLastFocused and getAll build their window objects from
  it where Chrome finds no WindowController, honouring windowTypes and
  populate. tabs.query({windowId}) matches the tabs of that window, and
  the tab objects of patch 0025 carry the window id through the
  SessionTabHelper.
- SetEmbedderActionPopupOpener(): where the profile has no Browser,
  action.openPopup() runs the embedder's opener on the active tab of the
  embedder's most recently focused (or the given) window. As in Chrome it
  fails for an unfocused window, a popup window, or a tab without a
  visible popup; the call resolves once the popup's page loaded.

Nothing changes when no embedder registers the hooks.
